{"diagnosis": "Recent results in this arm show a consistent asymmetry: capacity/depth cuts collapse exact (repair/cycle_region visits=2 -> 0.4707 vs 0.782 predicted; hidden=24 -> 0.5078 vs 0.78; stopping/horizon2 verifier_visits=0 -> 0.832 vs 0.918), while ldt_projection=true only marginally helps (0.7695 vs 0.80) and does not beat the incumbent. Crucially, the retrieval incumbent's own exact_by_visit is [0.9883, 0.9961, 0.9961]: the visit-1->2 gain is +0.0078 but visit-2->3 gain is exactly 0.0000. So the third visit is redundant for exactness, and the binding constraint is the visit-1->2 transition, not latent capacity or verifier feedback. Removing visits 2->3 is therefore the highest-value FLOPs cut, while hidden/verifier cuts are risky (evidence shows they drop exact by 0.1-0.3). Predicted gains must beat 0.9961 by >0.005 or match within 0.005 with >=10% fewer FLOPs.",
  "proposals": [
    {"config": {"visits": 2}, "rationale": "Incumbent exact_by_visit is [0.9883,0.9961,0.9961]: visit 3 adds zero exactness (delta=0.0000) while visit 2 carries the full gain. Cutting visits 3->2 removes one full TRM visit, cutting FLOPs per instance by ~1/3 (3,346,176 -> ~2.23M, ~33% fewer, well above the 10% threshold) with no expected exactness loss. Params unchanged (11,683).", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.9955, "falsification": "If measured dev_exact < 0.991 (i.e., drops >0.005 below 0.9961), the visit-3 redundancy hypothesis is refuted and the proposal should be rejected."},
    {"config": {"hidden": 24}, "rationale": "Params scale roughly as hidden^2 in the mixer/latent nets; hidden 32->24 gives (24/32)^2 = 0.5625x on those terms, empirically ~6,843 params (~41% fewer). The retrieval incumbent is at 0.9961 with a 0.0034 ECE, so a modest capacity cut may be absorbed by the redundancy in the relation+mean aggregation; exact_by_visit shows the answer state is already converged by visit 2, suggesting the head is not capacity-limited.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.994, "falsification": "If measured dev_exact < 0.991 or params are not materially below 11,683, the capacity-headroom hypothesis is refuted; do not promote."},
    {"config": {"latent_steps": 3}, "rationale": "Transitive dependency closure requires multi-hop propagation through the relation matrix; latent_steps=2 -> 3 adds one more latent net evaluation per visit (FLOPs +50% on the latent branch, params unchanged ~11,683). The incumbent is at the ceiling (0.9961), so extra latent depth targets the residual 0.0034 ECE/0.0039 miss mass via deeper transitive propagation.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.997, "falsification": "If measured dev_exact <= 0.9961 (no gain over incumbent) or ECE does not improve, the extra latent depth is refuted and the proposal should be rejected."}
  ]}
